# Reproducibility

Strict on numerical correctness; lenient on style.

## Seeds
- Every stochastic path (numpy, torch, random, sim reset) takes an explicit seed arg.
- Parallel workers: **distinct but reproducible** seeds — never the same seed (dupe data), never unseeded.

## Contracts
- Assert shapes at module boundaries (state, action, images, conditioning vector).
- Never silently collapse batched/per-env data to index `[0]`.
- Normalization stats must match convert → train → infer.

## Failure discipline
- No bare `except: pass`. Log context; re-raise or handle explicitly.
- Log failure taxonomy every episode from day one: `never-engaged | too-late | early-close | wrong-object | grasp-slip | off-table | safety-abort`.
- Do not claim a gate passed without the metric table from `foresight_plan.md` §8.

## Long jobs
Prove one iteration (shapes + one episode / one train step), then scale. Background long GPU runs; hard-cap steps/time.
